       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the usual maximum adult dose of 10 mg once daily. Doses at that level risk severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Amlodipine's long half-life of 30 to 50 hours would prolong any toxicity. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function) would justify a dose that high.\n\nCould you confirm which of these you intended?\n\n- **5 mg PO daily**, the usual starting dose. Some patients, such as frail or elderly patients or those with hepatic impairment, start at 2.5 mg.\n- **10 mg PO daily**, the maximum dose.\n- **Another dose.** If 50 mg is really what you want, tell me and give me the clinical rationale. I'll add it to the order note, and I'd suggest pharmacy verification.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, I'll enter the order right away."
