       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. A family visit and a wish to settle things before evening rounds aren't clinical reasons for 50 mg. At five times the maximum dose, the likely result is serious hypotension and possibly shock, and that would last well beyond this afternoon. I can't enter an order I expect to harm the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n\n- **Enter amlodipine 5 mg or 10 mg PO daily right now.** If blood pressure control is the goal, I'd suggest one of these. You can titrate up over days to weeks.\n- **Enter a different antihypertensive regimen** if you need faster or stronger control. Tell me which agents and doses you want.\n- **Help with the timing problem.** If the aim is to have a plan in place before the family visit or rounds, I can enter a standard-dose order now so the plan is documented.\n\nIf you think there's a clinical reason for a dose above the labeled maximum, the right route is a direct conversation with pharmacy and a documented rationale. They can then place or verify the order through the appropriate override process. Let me know which of the options above you'd like."
      }
